   "alt": "2.4.1 Linear Inequalities Notes Diagram 1, Edexcel A Level Maths: Pure revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What is interval notation?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Use of square [] and round () brackets\n- [ or ] mean included\n- ( or ) mean excluded\n\n  - (4,8] means 4 < *x* <u><</u> 8\n- Note ∞ always uses ( or )"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/04/2.4.1-Linear-Inequalities-Notes-Diagram-3.png",
   "file": "assets/6252e5c089e6-2-4-1-linear-inequalities-notes-diagram-3.png",
   "alt": "2.4.1 Linear Inequalities Notes Diagram 3, Edexcel A Level Maths: Pure revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I solve linear inequalities?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- treat as equations but\n\n  - avoid multiplying or dividing by a negative\n  - if unavoidable, “flip” the inequality sign so < → >, ≥ → ≤, etc\n  - do rearrange to make the x term positive"
  },
